  forms will need display code regardless — but keeping it a separate layer over a pure core means the validation rules
  stay testable without a browser, which matters more here given there's no test setup yet.

[38;5;246m⏺ [39mUser answered Claude's questions:
[38;5;246m  ⎿  · How should the shared validation surface handle error reporting and display? → Pure core + display helper[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Third question — the delivery format, which is the one real structural constraint in this repo. [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is a plain
  [38;5;153m<script src>[39m global; [38;5;153msrc/[39m uses CommonJS [38;5;153mrequire[39m. There's no bundler, so a shared module has to pick how it's loaded.

  [1mThe fork:[0m how the validation module gets into the browser page and into a test runner.

  - [1mDual export shim[0m ([38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m if present, else attach to [38;5;153mwindow[39m) — buys: [38;5;153mindex.html[39m keeps working when opened
    straight from disk, and Node can [38;5;153mrequire()[39m the module for tests. Costs: four lines of boilerplate at the bottom of
    the file, a slightly dated idiom. Easy to drop later.
  - [1mES modules[0m ([38;5;153mexport[39m + [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m) — buys: the modern, clean idiom, no shim. Costs: the page stops working
    over [38;5;153mfile://[39m (module loading is blocked there), so you'd need [38;5;153mnpx serve[39m or similar to view it, and [38;5;153msrc/[39m's CommonJS
    files can't [38;5;153mrequire()[39m it without converting them too. Reversing this means touching the HTML and the test setup.
  - [1mBrowser global only[0m ([38;5;153mwindow.Validation = …[39m) — buys: simplest, matches [38;5;153mapp.js[39m exactly today. Costs: not loadable in
    Node, so the validator can't be unit-tested without a DOM shim — which undercuts the point of keeping the core pure.

  [1mMy recommendation: the dual export shim.[0m It's the only option that keeps the demo page openable as-is [3mand[0m lets the
  pure core be tested in plain Node — and the shim is trivially deletable if you later add a bundler.
